  "summary": "The classic 68.6 x 53.3 mm UNO outline with a 32-bit RA4M1, a 12 x 8 red LED matrix and an ESP32-S3 for WiFi.",
  "description": "The UNO outline with USB-C, a 12 × 8 LED matrix and Wi-Fi. Mounting holes and shield headers follow the UNO layout; component heights are approximate.",
  "confidence": "datasheet",
  "source": "Mechanical figures from Arduino's ABX00087 Product Reference Manual, section 13 'Mounting Holes And Board Outline' (PDF dated 22/06/2023): the drawing was measured from its vector paths rather than read off the picture, giving a 68.58 x 53.34 mm outline with the notched right end and four holes dimensioned at 15.24 mm and 13.97 mm from the left end, 50.80 mm apart, plus 66.04 mm along and 17.78 mm and 45.72 mm across, each hole called out R1.60 (3.2 mm). Those six numbers are the UNO R3 pattern exactly once the figure is turned to match the pinout, so the outline, the holes and the five header rows are the same as arduino-uno-r3; the header positions themselves are not dimensioned anywhere in the datasheet. Component positions come from the same document's section 12 pinout illustration, which was checked to scale (it measures 1.2895 tall/wide against the true 1.2857) and read off at 300 dpi: USB-C centre 38.03 mm across, barrel jack centre 8.4 mm across and 11.5 mm in, ESP32-S3-MINI 20.3 x 15.5 mm flush with the USB end, RA4M1 10 x 10 mm, the 12 x 8 matrix on a 2.13 mm pitch from 33.6 to 58.4 mm along and 11.0 to 27.3 mm across, the reset button 9.3 x 6.0 mm and the Qwiic socket 5.4 x 6.3 mm at the far end. Not verified: no figure anywhere gives the barrel jack, button, module or matrix heights, so those are typical values for the part type; board thickness 1.6 mm is the standard UNO figure rather than a dimensioned value; the three OFF/GND/VRTC pads beside the power header are placed from the pinout picture only; and no board current is published, so none is quoted. Arduino's own copy of the PDF answers this client with HTTP 403, so the document read was a byte-for-byte retailer mirror of the same ABX00087 file.",
